# system/net-allow.list — every door of this machine, the one list. setup.sh makes the firewall
# from it (lib/net.sh); verify, the report and tools/portscan.sh hold the machine against it.
#
#   PORT/PROTO  WHERE  WHEN    WHAT
#
# WHERE  world  anyone on the internet (and the LAN)
#        lan    private addresses only: the firewall's zone kawa-lan (lib/net.sh, NET_LAN_SOURCES)
#        local  this computer only: bound to its loopback, no firewall needed
#        shut   a program binds it on every address; the firewall keeps it closed
# WHEN   always
#        ssh    SSH_SERVER=yes and a key in ~/.ssh/authorized_keys (keys only: no key, no sshd)
#        remote the remote page is installed (fk-remote.service)
6881/tcp    world  always  torrents: peers connect in
6881/udp    world  always  torrents: DHT and uTP
53317/tcp   lan    always  LocalSend: files coming in
53317/udp   lan    always  LocalSend: devices finding each other
8737/tcp    lan    remote  the remote page
22/tcp      lan    ssh     SSH, keys only
546/udp     lan    always  DHCPv6: the router's answers
53/tcp      local  always  systemd-resolved: names, for this computer
53/udp      local  always  systemd-resolved: names, for this computer
323/udp     local  always  chrony's control port
9696/tcp    local  always  Prowlarr
11434/tcp   local  always  Ollama: the update's local fixer
68/udp      shut   always  DHCP: the answers follow our own requests
5353/udp    shut   always  mDNS: browsers and Steam listen; nothing here answers it
27036/tcp   shut   always  Steam: Remote Play, never opened
27036/udp   shut   always  Steam: Remote Play discovery, never opened
